OL,3,CWife killer Glyn Razzell to remain in
OL,4,Cprison after High Court ruling
OL,6,FKiller Glyn Razzell, who murdered his
OL,7,Festranged wife in 2002, will remain in
OL,8,Fprison after the Parole Board's
OL,9,Fdecision to release him on licence was
OL,10,Freversed at the High Court.
OL,12,FRazzell was jailed for life with a
OL,13,Fminimum of almost 16 years in 2003 for
OL,14,Fthe murder of Linda Razzell, who
OL,15,Fdisappeared on her way to work at
OL,16,FSwindon College, Wiltshire, during
OL,17,Ftheir divorce proceedings.
OL,19,FThe mother of four's body has never
OL,20,Fbeen found.
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G1/4
